                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The total game completion time was about: 30 or 40 seconds. basically, there is no story. You start glitched under the floor,wasd to move and arrow keys to look around. I got unglitched by nocliping outside of the room, and back in through thewindow. There is a british guy there talking to you, he's the hotel room manager or whatever. He gives you a warning andtells you to turn out the lights. As soon as the lights go out, you see red eyes above the hotel's servant's shoulder, that \nthen rushes at you with a growl, and you are then sent back to the home menu. \n\nThis is a nice little project that anyone could build on in unreal engine, which is fairly easy to use. Whoever made this did a nice job with the textures and furniture. Neat idea!\n\nI do not recommend this game, because it is not a game at all. With or without a VR headset, the things i said still apply. I do not recommend this because it is kinda pointless. I get it is a test, an experiament, but it is really pointless.",
